docs/media/final and docs/media/rf hold renders of LAFAN1 motions (© 2018 Ubisoft Entertainment; CC BY-NC-ND 4.0;
https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-animation-dataset), retargeted to the G1 (LAFAN1 Retargeting Dataset),
resampled, cut to 10 s and rendered. They are for non-commercial illustration only and are not covered by the MIT
license in LICENSE.

docs/media/boxing holds a render of InterHuman clip 1566 (https://github.com/tr3e/InterGen; CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), both people
retargeted to the G1 with HoloRetarget and rendered. It is shared under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/) and is not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/musclevae holds renders of policies tracking the walk and run clips of MuscleVAE
(https://github.com/wangchek/MuscleVAE_, whose repository has no license): LAFAN1 motions (© 2018 Ubisoft Entertainment;
CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) retargeted to its skeleton, drawn with the bone meshes of MASS (https://github.com/lsw9021/MASS;
Apache-2.0). They are for non-commercial illustration only and are not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/hoi holds renders of policies tracking the reference motions of twelve of HDMI's tasks
(https://github.com/LeCAR-Lab/HDMI, whose repository has no license), drawn with the robot and object models of its
release in the look of its simulation videos. They are for non-commercial illustration only and are not covered by the
MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/hand holds renders of a policy tracking SPIDER's kinematic retargets
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/retarget/retarget_full) of hand-object demonstrations from HRDexDB, OakInk and DexYCB,
with the retargets drawn over it, those datasets' object meshes and SPIDER's models of the XHand, the Allegro hand and the Inspire hand. They are for non-commercial
illustration only and are not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE. g1_walk_tea.webp and g1_walk_tea_wholebody.webp render policies tracking SPIDER's retarget
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/retarget/retarget_example) of a GigaHands demonstration (https://github.com/brown-ivl/gigahands;
CC BY-NC 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/) on Unitree's G1 model (BSD-3-Clause) with SPIDER's Inspire hands
on its wrists, after the G1 walks LAFAN1's walk1_subject1 (© 2018 Ubisoft Entertainment; CC BY-NC-ND 4.0;
https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-animation-dataset), retargeted to the G1 (LAFAN1 Retargeting Dataset); they are for
non-commercial illustration only and are not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/robokit holds renders of RoboKit's (https://github.com/openrobokit/robokit; MIT) G1 box carrying, G1 climbing and
Go2 jumping examples, planned on this library's world model and executed in MuJoCo Warp, with Unitree's G1 model
(BSD-3-Clause) and MuJoCo Menagerie's Unitree Go2 (https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie; BSD-3-Clause). The G1
climbing render tracks a climbing motion capture of OmniRetarget / Holosoma (https://github.com/amazon-far/holosoma;
Apache-2.0). The G1 box carrying render (g1_carry.webp, and its tile in grid.webp) tracks a clip of OMOMO
(https://github.com/lijiaman/omomo_release, whose data terms are not stated) that RoboKit retargets; it is for non-commercial
illustration only and is not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/quadrotor holds renders (and a grid of them) of policies tracking flights of Race Against the Machine
(https://github.com/tii-racing/drone-racing-dataset; Bosello et al., IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters 2024, and its piloted
race-track flights of release v3.0.0, Bosello et al., IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters 2026; the dataset by TII Racing, CC BY
4.0), the flown path and the gates drawn from its motion capture, with a model of its drone written in this repository from the
paper's specification. They are shared under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

docs/media/robomimic holds renders (and a grid of them) of policies tracking proficient-human demonstrations of robomimic
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/robomimic/robomimic_datasets; MIT; Mandlekar et al., CoRL 2021) in the scenes they were
recorded in, drawn with the models, meshes and textures of robosuite 1.5.0 (https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robosuite;
MIT), the demonstration laid over each in translucent blue.

docs/media/mbrl holds renders of mbrl-lib's (https://github.com/facebookresearch/mbrl-lib; MIT, Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc. and
its affiliates) cart-pole and pusher models, its cartpole.xml and pusher.xml, as its CEM controller executes in MuJoCo plans
made on this library's world model, drawn with this library's lights, floor and sky.

docs/media/wuji_piano holds a render of a policy trained here playing Eden's Ode to Joy arrangement
(https://github.com/embodied-ai-nexus/Eden; Copyright 2026 Kashu Yamazaki, Apache-2.0) on the passive keyboard of Eden's
assets (from RoboPianist, Copyright 2023 The RoboPianist Authors, Apache-2.0) with Wuji Technology's Wuji Hand 2 models
(https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description; MIT), and the piano roll of that episode. The sources' notices and
terms, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, are not replaced by this repository's LICENSE.

docs/media/teaser.webp puts 6 s of such renders in fourteen blocks. The LAFAN1 tracking block is under the terms of the
docs/media/final paragraph, the Two G1s block under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 as docs/media/boxing, the Muscles block under those of
docs/media/musclevae and the Hand-object block under those of docs/media/hand. The Human-object interaction block, renders of
four of HDMI's tasks, is under the terms of the docs/media/hoi paragraph, and the RoboKit planning block, the docs/media/robokit
renders of its three examples (G1 box carrying tracks the OMOMO clip), under the sources and terms that paragraph names. The
Racing quadrotor block holds renders like docs/media/quadrotor's, under CC BY 4.0 as that paragraph says, and the Adroit door
block a render of another policy trained here on the same demonstration and scene as the docs/media/adroit_door preview, under
the sources and terms of the Adroit Door paragraph below. The Adroit pen, hammer and relocate blocks hold
docs/media/adroit_suite renders, under the sources and terms of the Adroit suite paragraph below, and the Wuji piano block a
render of the docs/media/wuji_piano policy, under the sources and terms that paragraph names. The Manipulation block holds renders
like docs/media/robomimic's, under the sources and terms that paragraph names. The mbrl-lib planning block holds the
docs/media/mbrl renders; no other part of it is covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

The Adroit Door preview in docs/media/adroit_door shows a policy trained here to track a physical replay of DAPG's
clip 23 from door-v0_demos.pickle (https://github.com/aravindr93/hand_dapg, commit
9a1de23df6574e1b94e1da742e3326eb1f61c013; repository license: Apache-2.0). The native Adroit scene and visual assets
come from Gymnasium-Robotics 1.3.1 (https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/Gymnasium-Robotics; MIT,
Copyright (c) 2022 Farama Foundation). The demonstration archives, model XML, meshes and textures are obtained
separately and are not redistributed in this repository. Their original notices and terms are not replaced by
this repository's LICENSE.

The Adroit suite previews in docs/media/adroit_suite use Pen, Hammer and Relocate demonstrations from the same
DAPG commit and native Gymnasium-Robotics 1.3.1 assets credited above, under the same original notices and terms.
Their demonstration archives, model XML, meshes and textures are likewise supplied externally and not redistributed.
